Hi Alexandre,

Thanks for your reply, and for making your patches available. I'm glad
we can build on the same foundation.

I'll work from your v2 series, first separating the shared qemu-server
D-Bus display support from the console-specific parts. Then I'll rebase
the WebRTC console onto that base, using the per-VM bus from your
DBusDisplay.pm. I'll keep the media service in a separate package and
preserve your authorship on the original patches.

I'll also include the NVIDIA EGL readback fix I linked in my previous
mail, keeping the existing VAAPI path available. My testing of that fix
was limited to the capture/encoding adapter with output to a file; I
still need to check it through the full Kyber console in the browser.

I'll take the OpenGL 4.6 / Venus series you mentioned into account when
rebasing. The shared base will still need feedback from the Proxmox
developers on the configuration and integration.

No problem about your availability. I'll send the revised patches to
the list with you in Cc, so you can have a look when you have time.

Thanks,
Dmitry
